ta-1node.yaml` / `example-user-data-2node.yaml`\nremain for ad-hoc labs. Feed rendered YAML via vendor BMC, or apply manually and reboot."},"772":{"id":"/getting-started-44","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"Extra-var `apply_now=true` writes user-data on the node and can reboot it. Inference must already be stopped. Default is render-only."},"773":{"id":"/getting-started-45","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"To import prep from bootstrap: `--extra-vars run_cloud_init_prep=true`."},"774":{"id":"/getting-started-46","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"The playbook installs prereqs, highspeed netplan on 2+ nodes (from the generated per-node\nnetplan when present), K3s server on the **orchestrator** node (`role: orchestrator` in\n`lab.yaml`), agents, labels, kubeconfig."},"775":{"id":"/getting-started-47","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"Verify:"},"776":{"id":"/getting-started-48","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"Expected (2-node example):"},"777":{"id":"/getting-started-49","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"If NotReady: `journalctl -u k3s` on the node; re-run bootstrap. Guided printout: `bazelisk run //:manage -- setup`."},"778":{"id":"/getting-started-50","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["gett