hain is Linux-native). On Windows, clone on the WSL2 filesystem, not\n`/mnt/c`."],[621,"The **Workspaces** sidebar section (`#workspaces`) embeds Coder and Kasm in-tab when running, with per-service Helm start/stop toggles so you can reclaim \\~2 CPU / 4Gi per stack under tight capacity."],[36,"The `.bazelversion` pins the version."],[1877,"The `hermes-gateway` Endpoints IP is rendered at deploy time from the control-plane node InternalIP (`LAB_SPARK0_IP` override supported)."],[742,"The `lab.yaml` topology file for all five configurations (1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 nodes)"],[126,"The BATS tests mock external commands (including kubectl) so they never touch real clusters or credentials."],[121,"The classic make-based paths remain for compatibility/legacy."],[399,"The container can reach LLM providers on the **host** at\n`http://host.docker.internal:<port>/v1` (LiteLLM/vLLM on the workstation) and\ncloud APIs (`api.x.ai`, …) over ordinary egress. `devcontainer.json` adds\n`host.docker.internal` → `host-gateway` so this works on Docker Desktop **and**\nLinux Engine. Do not use `--network=host`."],[602,"The container entrypoint applies Drizzle migrations to `DATABASE_URL` before starting the server."],[346,"The contributor image is **Linux multi-arch** (`linux/amd64` + `linux/arm64`). The same\n`.devcontainer/` definition runs on:"],[599,"The custom portal is a self-hosted **Next.js 16** application (`dashboard/`) with **better-auth** session protection and **Drizzle + SQLite** persistence for utility run history and preferences."],[3682,"The dashboard Deployment may mount the host Docker socket and `/mnt/models` so Tasks/Storage work. Anyone who can log in can stop containers and delete allow-listed files. Keep auth on; never set `AUTH_BYPASS` outside tests. SSO: SSO."],[637,"The dashboard utility `scripts/utilities/dev-workspaces.sh` wraps the same logic for the UI. RBAC in `k8s/dev/dashboard/rbac.yaml` grants the dashboard ServiceAccount Helm lifecycle in `coder` and `kasm`