d why heavy workloads are dangerous around power events"],[1071,"The host `hermes-lab` stack is a **persistent lab operator*&#x2A;. Coder and Kasm workspaces use a separate &#x2A;*`workspace-dev`** profile for coding assistance:"],[598,"The image starts Hermes `workspace-dev` in the background on session launch. Desktop shortcuts open the dashboard (`:9119`) and Hermes CLI."],[1878,"The lab portal **Agent Chat** panel shows prerequisites, deploy/stop controls, and launch links."],[2963,"The lab uses **production-grade Traefik v3** (official Helm chart) as the unified HTTPS entry point, with **Authelia** for user management and forward-auth SSO. K3s bundled Traefik stays disabled; the standalone Helm install supports CRD middleware chains, TLS, and metrics."],[68,"The MkDocs site published two aliases with **mike**; Fumadocs has no mike equivalent, so the\nsame URLs are produced by building the static export twice with different `basePath` values:"],[4355,"The model"],[4316,"The model is TP=1 (many Nemotron nano/super, Qwen3.6 dual, MedGemma)"],[1024,"The multi-arch **devcontainer** can install the Hermes **CLI** (`hermes`) for\nlocal agent-assisted coding — see dev-environment.md.\nThat is separate from this page’s **host Docker gateway** on DGX Spark nodes.\nNever commit API keys or `hermes/data/.env` from either path."],[2156,"The multi-arch `.devcontainer/` image (linux/amd64 + arm64) includes bazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, ruff, mypy, ansible, kubectl, helm, kubeconform, shellcheck, bats, yamllint, Node.js 22, Python 3.11, Playwright, and a pinned Grok Build CLI. Versions and checksums are pinned in `.devcontainer/tool-versions.env` (shared with CI). Independent fetch stages keep rebuilds local to the pin that changed. Works on Apple Silicon, Windows (Docker Desktop + WSL2), Linux, and DGX Spark. See dev-environment.md."],[1726,"The Next.js control plane includes an **Observability** section (`#observability`):"],[701,"The NVIDIA GPU Operator works well on K3s but:"],[2908,"The old 64Gi policy floor reserved \\~192 GiB across three Sparks before any Job, so Mode A (\\~189 GiB) always failed and operators clicked through. That made the guard a paper tiger."],[4299,"The orchestrator name (not \"spark0\") is what the generated inventory and `group_vars`\nuse for `k3s_control_plane`. Inventory: generated from `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml`\n(legacy hand-made example: `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini.example`)."],[50,"The output is at `docs/generated/shell/reference.md` and appears in the site under **Reference > Code-Generated Reference**."],[774,"The playbook installs prereqs, highspeed netplan on 2+ nodes (from the generated per-node\nnetplan when present), K3s server on the **orchestrator** node (`role: orchestrator` in\n`lab.yaml`), agents, labels, kubeconfig."],[94,"The previous short paragraph has been replaced by this more complete description."],[1274,"The proxy must stay up if backends are down (per-model 503 is fine)."],[209,"The Shell Commands & Helpers page is **not** written by hand. It is produced from structured comments inside the scripts."],[3388,"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."],[3382,"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"],[4263,"The switch is a managed 4-port 400G QSFP-DD device with a 10GbE management port:"],[4267,"The switch's management IP (e.g. `10.0.0.2`) is declared in the `switch:` block; only a\n**read-only** API probe may use it. The switch password is read from the\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` environment variable at runtime — never commit it."],[33,"The traditional Makefile and direct `ansible-playbook` / `./scripts/manage.sh` invocations remain available for compatibility and for people who have not installed bazelisk."],[63,"The visual suite serves the export itself (`playwright.config.mjs` `webServer` runs\n`scripts/serve_static.mjs`), so nothing has to be started by hand. It captures the ten pages\nwhose rendering carries risk — index, getting-started, architecture, models-catalog,\ntroubleshooting, reboot-safety, dgx-spark-notes, monitoring-observability, dev-workspaces,\ngitea-ci-setup — at both desktop and mobile widths, waits for hydration plus the client-side\nMermaid SVGs, and drives every animation and transition to its end state before capturing so\nbaselines are reproducible."],[5903,"THEME\\_STORAGE\\_KEY"],[6805,"themeId"],[5900,"ThemeMode"],[5650,"ThemeProvider"],[5657,"ThemeSelector"],[435,"Then install &#x2A;*Node 22+** and run `cd dashboard && npm ci`, plus `docs/setup-docs.sh` for the docs site."],[785,"Then reboot workers, then spark0. Jobs will **not** come back. Full sequence: Reboot safety · Patch and reboot."],[3763,"Theory"],[1609,"There is **no** official DeepSeek-V4.1 / V4.1-Pro checkpoint. Local DeepSeek on this lab is **V4.1-Flash only** (Mode C). Do not use `nvidia/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-NVFP4` (old 284B)."],[3881,"There is no `manage.sh sync-to-k8s` verb — sync is a dashboard action after login."],[1149,"These defaults protect SSH and the control plane on remotely managed GB10 nodes. Do not weaken them for demos."],[2018,"These principles override convenience. When in doubt, choose stability and explicit control."],[3526,"They do **not** start kimi, Mode B/C, or visual Deployments"],[3527,"They do **not** weaken `restartPolicy` or Resource Guard"],[2288,"Thin `main` + **BASH\\_SOURCE source guard** (enforced by `//tests:doc_coverage`)"],[2695,"Thin `main` + BASH\\_SOURCE source guard (see §6 skeleton)"],[2329,"Thin `main` + BASH\\_SOURCE source guard (utilities with `main()`)"],[2484,"Thin RSC composer — single `Promise.all` data load"],[5336,"Thin wrappers around scripts/lib/py/lab\\_topology.py: validate the declarative\nlab topology (ansible/inventory/lab.yaml), emit flat facts, and r